index 6065be1fca6946af05931088dcc21afdd78d505e..f4ba163dd0b9da22990e6a987aa1bbb3f85d6523 100644
--- a/README.md
+++ b/README.md
@@ -27,3 +27,12 @@ array position out of range or not canonical, `move` into its own child, `test`
 accepted only as the last token of an `add`/`copy`/`move` target. `remove` with the empty path is
 rejected, since the result would not be a JSON value. `test` compares objects regardless of member
 order. Pointers follow the rules of `resolvePointer` above.
+
+## JSON Merge Patch (RFC 7386)
+
+`applyMergePatch(target, patch)`, exported from `src/index.ts`, applies a JSON Merge Patch and returns
+the merged document. A patch that is not an object (including an array) replaces the target as a
+whole. An object patch is merged member by member: `null` removes the member, any other value is
+merged recursively, and a target that is not an object is treated as an empty object. Consequently a
+member cannot be set to `null` with a merge patch (use JSON Patch for that). Neither argument is
+mutated. It throws an `Error` if `target` or `patch` is not a JSON value.
